  "novel_mechanics_found": "ACTION7 has a narrower undo window than previously documented: it undoes an east-only carrier move when pressed immediately, but even adapter-state-silent ACTION6 clicks clear that pending undo. In the observed sequence, A1 moved only east/elevator carriers, ten repeated off-screen clicks changed no adapter state, and the following A7 was a no-op. A separate A1,A7,A7 probe showed the immediate A7 restoring the move and the second A7 doing nothing (no redo and no deeper undo stack). Negative findings: double-clicking every integer pixel in the full 6x6 world-coordinate footprint of the canonical east carrier and east peg caused no game-state or non-row-0 pixel change; continuous click paths between the peg and carrier, drag-like click sweeps across a visible ferry and its adjacent rail cell, and a right-to-left screen-pan-like sweep were also silent.",
  "narrative": "Precondition passed exactly as requested. resolve_replay_plan({\"game\":\"lf52\",\"levels_reproduced\":6}, Path(\".\")) resolved 615 labels from results/outer_loop_fable5_lf52_probe_l6_20260712.json. Replaying them from a fresh env.reset() reached frame_level=6, GameState.NOT_FINISHED, with the canonical L7 carrier configuration. Exploration then used 332 calls. First, every integer pixel in the predicted 6x6 footprint of the off-screen east carrier at grid (22,4) (pixel x=137..142,y=29..34) was double-clicked, then every pixel in the east peg footprint at (22,6) (x=137..142,y=41..46) was double-clicked; all 144 clicks were adapter-state-silent and changed only the cosmetic row-0 action bar. Next, six west moves brought the visible ferry to its left rail end and established an east left-packed state. Three bidirectional one-pixel click sweeps across the visible ferry and adjacent rail cell (x=11..22 at y=36,38,40; 72 clicks) produced no drag or selection. An ACTION7 interaction probe then found that ten silent repeated clicks after an effective A1 erase the pending undo, while an immediate A1,A7 pair does undo and a second A7 does not redo. A5 plus click (7,56) restored the canonical L7 state. Finally, continuous one-pixel vertical paths between the off-screen peg and carrier were tried at x=140 in both directions and at x=138 peg-to-carrier, followed by a 39-click right-to-left screen-pan-like sweep from x=63 to x=25 at y=32. None changed the adapter state or non-cosmetic frame. The sequence was checkpointed throughout to /tmp/codex55_lf52_candidate.json. No level was won; max_level_reached honestly remains 6, and the run ended at the canonical L7 start with 947 total env.step calls.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The required 615-action prefix independently reproduced level 6 in this run; reproduction_verified is false only because no new L7 win exists to reproduce.",
    "ACTION7 must be immediate: state-silent clicks clear its pending carrier undo. A second ACTION7 is not redo and did not traverse an older undo.",
    "The full 6x6 sub-cell footprints tested here used the registered adapter's world pixel coordinates plus the frame offset: carrier x=137..142,y=29..34 and peg x=137..142,y=41..46.",
    "Discrete ACTION6 events cannot encode a literal pointer-down/hold/pointer-up gesture. This run tested the harness-expressible approximations: repeated same-pixel clicks and contiguous one-pixel paths in both directions.",
    "All negative click claims ignore the cosmetic row-0 action odometer and require both unchanged registered adapter state and zero changed pixels below row 0.",
    "The final state is the canonical L7 start configuration because A5+(7,56) reset it before the last click-only probes, which were all silent.",
    "The three round-9-refuted directions were not retried: no carrier/peg direct leapfrog pair test, no cell-center off-screen sweep, and no east-configuration-to-west-piece dependency matrix."
  ],
